r.org/image/images/big/11610"}},{"id":"890241","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"892596","description":"Submerged rock at the bottom of the drop is a bad pinning spot.","caption":"Any Which Way You Lose @ 1800 CFS","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"James O’Brien","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/890241","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/890241"}},{"id":"2929","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5322","description":"","caption":"Satan's Garden","poi_name":"Satan's Garden","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":"635","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/2929","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/2929"}},{"id":"19377","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9707","description":"Middle line at about 1200- 3000 cfs\r\n","caption":"Satans Garden- Middle Line","poi_name":"Satans Garden","subject":"Charlie Simmons","author":"Charlie Simmons","poi_id":"635","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/19377","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/19377"}},{"id":"11609","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8779","description":"Satan's Garden River Left at high water level.","caption":"Satan's Garden - river left","poi_name":"Satan's Garden","subject":"Satan's Garden - river left","author":"Steve Flanagan","poi_id":"635","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11609","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11609"}},{"id":"11606","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"8779","description":"This \"Satan's Garden\" river right is a smooth slide/drop that puts you into a nice little eddie pool. ... Scout the 2nd rapid \"Every which way you loose\" downstream though - there were nasty potholes on the left, and the right side would be good if it wasn't for a deadly strainer on 16 Jul 05.","caption":"River Right - Satan's Garden","poi_name":"Satan's garden (River Right - 1st Falls)","subject":"Steve Flanagan","author":"Adam Martin","poi_id":"635","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/11606","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/11606"}},{"id":"19378","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9707","description":"river right line","caption":"Satans Garden- Right line","poi_name":"Satans Garden","subject":"Charlie Simmons","author":"Charlie Simmons","poi_id":"635","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/19378","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/19378"}}],"detail":{"id":"70","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"\"The Little Uchee is in Lee Co. The creek is a fall line whitewater run with a few good rapids. The water quality is mediocre and muddy when it's running. To my knowledge we have no gauge. I used the Mulberry River in Georgia as a gauge. If it was really high we continued on to the Little Uchee. Unfortunately few boaters know of the Mulberry so it's of no aid. The access is on state road right of way. The first rapid \"Satan's Garden\" (at least that is what I think it was called) is a large river wide waterfall \\[known as Great Falls on the map\\]. There are lots of possible routes. Some are more painful than others. The other rapid that sticks in mind was \"Any which way you lose\" and it was near the end. I recall some nasty pot holes in the drop. It's probably not that hard a run I haven't been down there since I moved to Clemson some years ago. I'd say class III maybe IV.\" by Will Reeves\n\nSee also [www.alabamawhitewater.com](http://www.alabamawhitewater.com/guide/guide_files2/littleuchee.htm).","averageGradient":"50","maxGradient":null,"length":"1.3","correlations":[{"reachID":"70","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowR